<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Barnex half yr share moves further into red.</title>
<headline>Barnex half yr share moves further into red.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)     36.3 loss   vs   10.2 loss</p>
<p>    Investment income	  1.53	 vs    1.98</p>
<p>    Interest paid		nil	  vs    0.03</p>
<p>    Net funding		  7.49	 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Provision against loan   1.17	 vs    0.71</p>
<p>    Exploration expenditure  1.21	 vs    3.38</p>
<p>    Loss after excepts	 8.87	 vs    2.48</p>
<p>Full name: Barnato Exploration Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said its funds were being depleted by increased exploration activity -- particularly on the Prestea project in Ghana. An assessment of Barnex's exploration strategy and funding requirements were nearing completion and decision on how and to what extent the company should be refinanced would be taken in the near future.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
